<title>PERU: Southern Peru mulls dividends.</title>
<headline>Southern Peru mulls dividends.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's largest miner, Southern Peru Copper Corporation, will discuss July 30 setting a dividend for its common shares traded in New York, the Lima Stock Exchange reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>The corporation will also decide on setting a dividend for the labor shares of its wholly-owned subsidiary Southern Peru Ltd, which trades on the Lima bolsa, the stock exchange said.</p>
<p>Southern Peru Copper Corp is 54.1 pct owned by ASARCO Inc and 13.9 percent owned by Phelps Dodge Corp.</p>
<p>The company's copper production accounts for about 60 percent of Peru's total output.</p>
<p>((-- Marco Aquino, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
